program	closure_captures_reference_param_escaping_error.saw
triple	arm64-apple-darwin
twin	same
expect	error
build	refused	an escaping closure cannot capture `r`, a reference (`&Thing`) — a reference borrows storage for the duration of one call and may not outlive the frame it points into
meets_expect	yes
log	"error: an escaping closure cannot capture `r`, a reference (`&Thing`) — a reference borrows storage for the duration of one call and may not outlive the frame it points into"
log	"  --> examples/closure_captures_reference_param_escaping_error.saw:20:12"
log	"     |"
log	" 20 |     return { r.x + 1 }"
log	"     |            ^"
log	"   hint: pass the closure straight to the call that runs it (a non-escaping closure keeps its environment on the stack, so borrowing the frame is sound), or copy the values it needs out of the referent into locals ahead of the closure and capture those"
log	""
log	"error: an escaping closure cannot capture `m`, a reference (`&var Thing`) — a reference borrows storage for the duration of one call and may not outlive the frame it points into"
log	"  --> examples/closure_captures_reference_param_escaping_error.saw:25:13"
log	"     |"
log	" 25 |     let f = { m.x + 1 }"
log	"     |             ^"
log	"   hint: pass the closure straight to the call that runs it (a non-escaping closure keeps its environment on the stack, so borrowing the frame is sound), or copy the values it needs out of the referent into locals ahead of the closure and capture those"
log	""
log	"2 error(s) generated"
